263
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:27,310
Oh. Huh.

264
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:31,570
Oh, it's, ew, used.

265
00:16:33,150 --> 00:16:35,320
Uh, cool.

266
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:43,160
I have just a few questions to ask, so I'll get out my official forms.

267
00:16:46,670 --> 00:16:48,580
So question one:

268
00:16:49,290 --> 00:16:53,130
You were married to Frances' daughter, Lilly. Correct?

269
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,380
Yes, I was.

270
00:16:55,550 --> 00:16:58,930
Okay, um, question two: Um, did that marriage end...

271
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:00,760
...A, happily...

272
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:03,310
...B, medium...

273
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:06,730
...or, C, in the total abandonment...

274
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:09,020
...of her and her two children?

275
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,110
It really says that?

276
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:12,440
Yeah, see?

277
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:16,820
I guess then I would have to say C.

278
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:20,120
Total abandonment.

279
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:23,410
Reasons for abandonment:

280
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:27,000
Um, A, top secret government work...

281
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:28,710
...B, amnesia...

282
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:32,250
...or, C, you're just a selfish, irresponsible...

283
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:34,880
...bad, bad man.

284
00:17:35,470 --> 00:17:37,880
I don't want the lipstick that much.

285
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:42,930
Would you do me a favor?

286
00:17:43,180 --> 00:17:44,890
Would you give Lilly...

287
00:17:45,850 --> 00:17:47,770
...that, please? What?

288
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:50,190
When you see Lilly, give her that note.

289
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:52,860
I wanted to talk to her at the memorial...

290
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:58,110
...but I pictured her getting mad the way you did, and I chickened out.

291
00:17:58,820 --> 00:18:01,320
I wrote her a note. Give it to her, please?

292
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:04,160
But you came to see Lilly?

293
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:06,250
Yeah. Why?

294
00:18:07,330 --> 00:18:09,170
Lilly's dead.

295
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:11,830
She what?

296
00:18:12,210 --> 00:18:13,250
She's dead.

297
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:14,960
Are you sure?

298
00:18:15,130 --> 00:18:18,260
If she isn't, cremating her was a big mistake.

299
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:22,510
I can't believe this. I just can't believe...

300
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:25,520
How? Oh, my God.

301
00:18:26,310 --> 00:18:27,350
How long ago?

302
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,190
Seventeen years ago.

303
00:18:29,350 --> 00:18:30,940
Oh.

304
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:33,940
What about the girls?

305
00:18:36,860 --> 00:18:40,700
Well, Ursula is a waitress and she lives in Soho.

306
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,410
And Phoebe...

307
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,950
...is on this couch.

308
00:18:55,630 --> 00:18:59,380
Yep, lipstick and a daughter. Big day for you.

309
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:03,470
Phoebe, I, um...

310
00:19:03,640 --> 00:19:05,140
Whoops.

311
00:19:06,100 --> 00:19:09,270
It's just, I don't know what to say.

312
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:15,400
I just can't believe that you're my daughter. You're so pretty.

313
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:19,440
Yes, well, that's neither here nor there.

314
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:24,530
Would it make you feel better if I said...

315
00:19:24,780 --> 00:19:28,370
...that I was very, very sorry I left?

316
00:19:30,750 --> 00:19:33,960
It doesn't matter what you say. It won't make a difference.

317
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:35,670
So you can just go.

318
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:42,470
Well, you know, in my defense, I was a lousy father.

319
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:45,430
- That's your defense?     - Yes, it is.

320
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:49,680
I burned the formula, and I put your diapers on backwards.

321
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:54,480
I made up a song to sing to you, but that made you cry even more.

322
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,560
You make up songs?

323
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:59,900
Well, no, just that one. But it was stupid.

324
00:20:00,150 --> 00:20:02,950
Let's see, how did it go? Um...

325
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:07,370
Sleepy girl, sleepy girl

326
00:20:07,990 --> 00:20:10,790
Why won't you go to sleep?

327
00:20:11,370 --> 00:20:14,080
Sleepy girl, sleepy girl

328
00:20:14,330 --> 00:20:16,460
You're keeping me up

329
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:37,440
I'm not very good at this.

330
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:42,030
Well, I am.

331
00:20:47,660 --> 00:20:48,700
Not yet. No.

332
00:20:54,370 --> 00:20:55,410
Hey.

333
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:57,420
Hey! How'd the audition go?

334
00:20:57,830 --> 00:20:59,250
Estelle said I didn't get it.

335
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:02,710
What? Why? Joey, you were so ready for it.

336
00:21:03,010 --> 00:21:04,340
I thought so too...

337
00:21:04,590 --> 00:21:07,220
...but the casting people had problems with me.

338
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:08,640
What kind of problem?

339
00:21:08,970 --> 00:21:11,560
To tell you the truth...

340
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:14,020
...they had a problem with the bag!     - Oh, my God!

341
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:18,100
You know what? It was a stupid play anyway.

342
00:21:19,060 --> 00:21:20,820
It's time to give up the bag.

343
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,610
I don't want to give up the bag.

344
00:21:24,110 --> 00:21:26,610
I don't have to give it up, do I, Rach?

345
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:32,450
You think I should give up the bag!

346
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:37,160
Joey, I'm sorry. As terrific as I think you are with it...

347
00:21:39,330 --> 00:21:44,050
...I just don't know if the world is ready for you and your bag.

348
00:21:46,550 --> 00:21:48,130
I can't believe this!

349
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:51,550
Wait, I'm not saying you shouldn't have a bag.

350
00:21:52,810 --> 00:21:56,980
There are other bags that are maybe a little less...

351
00:21:57,770 --> 00:21:59,270
...controversial.

352
00:22:00,310 --> 00:22:02,980
Yeah, um, they're called wallets.

